From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roshan Gautam <roshangautam07@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:47:04 +0545
Subject: [PATCH 02/74] deps: update llhttp to 9.4.3

Node.js 18 shipped llhttp 6.1.1, which terminates an HTTP/1 header block
on "\r\n\rX" instead of "\r\n\r\n". That allows request smuggling and
proxy-based access control bypasses (CVE-2025-23167). Node.js 20 fixed
this by moving to llhttp 9; do the same here, using the 9.4.3 tree that
the v20.x/v22.x security releases ship.

The node_http_parser.cc glue combines the upstream changes made for the
llhttp 8 and 9 upgrades: the new llhttp_settings_t layout (with the
on_chunk_extension callback kept for the chunk extension size limit),
the additional leniency flags enabled by --insecure-http-parser, and
contiguous indices for http.METHODS.

CVE-ID: CVE-2025-23167
Refs: https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/may-2025-security-releases
Refs: fd36a8dadba7 (deps: update llhttp to 8.1.0)
Refs: 190e45a291ef (deps: update llhttp to 9.1.2)
